# Security

## Multi-tenant

- Every query and mutation scopes by `organizationId` (and `projectId` when obra-scoped).
- Never trust client-supplied org/project ids without membership checks.

## Evidence (R2)

- Private objects only; use short-lived signed URLs.
- Validate type/size before upload.
- Do not expose permanent public bucket URLs.

## AuthZ

- Separate permissions: register vs approve vs administer.
- Allow immediate disable of offboarded users.
- MFA for admins can wait until MVP commercial; design sessions revocable now.

## Secrets

- `.env*` gitignored; Railway/Cloudflare secrets for deploy.
- No secrets in client bundles (`NUXT_PUBLIC_*` only for non-sensitive values).

## Personal data (Perú)

- Phones, names, roles, conversations, business docs — minimize retention; plan export/delete paths.
- Log access to sensitive exports.
